    "owner_words": "I want to get the mini-apps redone into a framework - it makes sense - i like symfony, its a good example | don't constrain it too much - this is a big task | you bring up something important - plans (contracts) at every level | these contracts and their economics are important | yes - but framework first",
    "dated": "2026-08-29",
    "source": "owner 2026-08-29; ops/docs/scratch/agentscient-framework-plan.md"
  },
  "premises": [
    {"text": "The dev lane's mini-apps are separate programs whose boundaries grew by accretion rather than from one framework contract.", "tag": "read", "source": "ops/docs/scratch/agentscient-framework-plan.md §1"},
    {"text": "A compiled container can refuse registry, dependency, tag-flow, and interface defects before the first capability runs.", "tag": "read", "source": "ops/docs/scratch/agentscient-framework-plan.md §2"},
    {"text": "Plans are prose documents with closed sidecars and child plans are digest-bound projections of parent units.", "tag": "read", "source": "ops/docs/scratch/agentscient-framework-plan.md §3"}
